From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 19:40:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] art: riscv64 asm without Zba/Zbb when the target lacks them

Zba/Zbb instructions in the riscv64 entrypoints and nterp go through
asm_support_riscv64.S macros (SHADD, SHADD_UW, ZEXT_W, SEXT_B,
ANDNOT): the single instruction under __riscv_zba / __riscv_zbb, so a
target with the extensions assembles to the same bytes; a base-ISA
sequence otherwise. Every nterp handler still fits 128 bytes at
rv64gc (largest 126, after linker relaxation).

Licence of the patched files: Apache-2.0 (their AOSP headers).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AOSP targets rv64gcv_zba_zbb_zbs]
Patch-Reason: a second riscv64 host target is plain rv64gc (a board without Zba/Zbb/Zbs), where the assembler rejects these instructions and libart cannot build; the march is the target, and nothing outside the source can replace the instructions
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
